/* ============================================================================
 * SPEED 2026-10-28 — PER-RESTAURANT LOCK (root cause of "save / print / KOT move take time")
 * Every order, KOT, bill, print-queue and transfer write used LockService.getScriptLock(): ONE lock for the
 * whole script, i.e. for ALL restaurants. The POS print station alone takes it every 1.5 s per client, so
 * one client's saves queued behind every other client's saves and print polls ("Lock timeout",
 * "PRINT_QUEUE_BUSY", 17-170 s answers). Now each request locks only ITS OWN restaurant: a short lease in
 * CacheService, claimed and released under the script lock for a few milliseconds. Same API as a Lock
 * (tryLock / waitLock / hasLock / releaseLock, re-entrant inside one execution). Time triggers and other
 * code that runs without a request client keep the real script lock. Client provisioning keeps it too.
 * ========================================================================== */
